task.description:
WF-03 Step 2 (Solution Design) for GitHub issue #402 (T010 hardcoded-UUID residual-29 migration). Produce a Type E prose fix design at src/design/iss0121_residual29_migration.md that:

(a) cites TestHarness.newUuid (helpers.zig:467) and TestHarness.newUuidString (helpers.zig:479) as the migration API and explicitly forbids any new helper, wrapper, or module;
(b) batches the 29 residual files into 4 BACKEND-DEV-friendly PRs of roughly equal size (8/8/8/5 files; 27/79/53/9 active T010 literals) with explicit per-batch file sets and per-file per-call replacement strategy (newUuid vs newUuidString, defer allocator.free for strings, preserve the all-zero sentinel where the API contract requires it);
(c) gives the four per-file replacement patterns (P1 instance-id, P2 actor-id typed [16]u8, P3 audit-id, P4 module-const forbidden) with binding-shape text snippets (NOT implementation code);
(d) defines four per-batch validation gates (G1 lint strictly decreases; G2 zig build test exits 0; G3 focused integration; G4 full integration suite) and a stale-inventory handling rule that forbids refreshing tools/lint_test_isolation.baseline.json to mask new violations;
(e) explicitly forbids promoting T010 from MAJOR to BLOCKER in tools/lint_test_isolation.py until the live lint reports MAJOR < 10 across the entire tests/integration tree (the deferred goal of the run — the single acceptable lint-side edit is the one-line severity change at tools/lint_test_isolation.py:84, performed as the last step of Batch D);
(f) names the post-fix verification recipe (python3 tools/lint_test_isolation.py tests/integration → MAJOR < 10; zig build test → exit 0; full integration suite → exit 0);
(g) treats T020 (module-level mutable var) and T050 (no BPM_TEST_DB_URL reference) findings as out-of-scope — they are separately actionable lint defects and require architectural changes beyond UUID isolation;
(h) does NOT contain implementation code (no Zig function bodies, no SQL DDL, no linter regex rewrites, no baseline JSON diffs).

Implementation MUST NOT begin until CODE-DESIGN-VALIDATOR (WF-03 Step 2b — hard gate) returns PASS. After validator PASS, BACKEND-DEV (WF-03 Step 3) applies the design mechanically per §5 (batches) and §6 (per-file patterns), running §7 validation gates after each batch.
